# API Design Principles

Follow these principles when designing and implementing APIs.

## RESTful Design

- Use appropriate HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE).
- Follow REST conventions for resource naming and structure.
- Use meaningful resource names.
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes.
- Version APIs appropriately.

## API Consistency

- Maintain consistent naming conventions across endpoints.
- Use consistent response formats.
- Follow consistent error handling patterns.
- Document APIs thoroughly.
- Include examples in API documentation.

## Request/Response Design

- Use clear, descriptive endpoint names.
- Implement proper request validation.
- Return consistent response structures.
- Include relevant metadata in responses.
- Use pagination for list endpoints.

## Error Handling

- Return appropriate HTTP status codes.
- Provide meaningful error messages.
- Include error details in consistent format.
- Log errors appropriately for debugging.
- Don't expose sensitive information in error responses.
